id: lightspeed-mode-gear-shift
name: Gear Shift
order: 1
slot: trait
description: >
  You are able to ramp up your speed at-will, allowing you to move faster than anyone else.
text: >
  Gear Shift: You are able to ramp up your speed at-will, allowing you to move faster than anyone else.
  (1)-[Passive]: Increase your Initiative Value by G(T).
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase the Tier of Power Extra Dice applied to your Strike and Dodge Rolls by G Dice Categories (min. 1d4).
  (3)-[Graded]: Lightspeed Mode has 2 Grades. Each Lightspeed Mode Grade:
  • Has its own Stress Test Requirement.
  • Has its own Tier of Power Requirement, which is equal to the Grade number (i.e. Grade 2 has a Tier of Power Requirement of 2+ and Grade 3 has a Tier of Power Requirement of 3+).
  • Sets the AMB (Attribute Modifier Bonus) of Lightspeed for the listed Attribute to the amount listed on the Grades table.
  • Increases the amount of Damage you suffer from Collision and Attacking Maneuvers by an amount listed on the Grades table.
  • Applies additional Aspects; some Grades have additional Aspects.

---

# (1) Initiative Value G(T).
[passive, effect 1]
initiative += $G * 1(T);

# (2) The Tier of Power Extra Dice of your Strike and Dodge Rolls G Categories higher.
[passive, effect 2]
dice.extra.strike.category += $G;
dice.extra.dodge.category += $G;

# (3) Its Grade's extra Damage, from Collision and Attacking Maneuvers alike (its table), 2(bT) less with FTL (3).
[automatic/being-hit, effect 3]
if ($G == 1) {
    incoming.damage += 2(bT) - min($M, 1) * 2(bT);
}
if ($G == 2) {
    incoming.damage += 5(bT) - min($M, 1) * 2(bT);
}
if ($G == 3) {
    incoming.damage += 6(bT) - min($M, 1) * 2(bT);
}
if ($G == 4) {
    incoming.damage += 8(bT) - min($M, 1) * 2(bT);
}
